n: Checking is the superior play here. Since the pot is small (limped pre-flop) and I am out of position or acting first, checking allows me to see the Turn card for free (infinite pot odds). This "free card" play lets me realize my substantial equity without bloating the pot with a hand that is currently only high-card value. If I bet, I risk getting raised or calling a bet when I am statistically an underdog to a made pair. Checking disguises the strength of my draw and keeps the pot controllable.\n\nAnswer: 0'}
