 aligns with a conservative strategy given my overall winnings. It\'s the most logical move here.  Let the Small Blind limp.\n\nSo, I\'m going with **Check**.\n\n\n', 'output': 'Evaluation: You are holding Queen of Spades and 9 of Diamonds (Q9 offsuit). In a heads-up scenario, this is a median-strength hand (around top 43%). While it has reasonable high-card value, it is not strong enough to confidently build a large pot pre-flop, especially if you are likely to be out of position post-flop. The availability of the "Check" option suggests you can see the flop for free (likely as the Big Blind facing a limp).\n\nReason: Raising with Q9o creates a larger pot where you may be dominated by better Queens or Pairs, and forces you to play aggressively out of position. Since you are currently in the lead in the overall match, a low-variance strategy is preferred. Checking allows you to see the community cards for free and re-evaluate without risking more chips on a speculative hand.\n\nAnswer: 0'}
